  "notes": "⛔ `low` because the research marks this entry medium-low and says outright that the parameters are largely inferred [LOW-CONF]. Read every number below as a reading of the released records, not a sourced measurement. What IS specific in the research is one structural claim, and it is the only claim this file leans on: \"melodic interest carried by the 808's pitch movement\" over a single pluck/bell motif with no pad. That inverts the usual roles, so `bassline.rhythm` is `independent_riff` with `followRootsProb` 0.5 — the lowest in this batch by a wide margin — while the melody gets a tight 4–6-pitch riff contour at 0.78. The 808 is bouncy rather than crushing: short-to-mid decay, fast repeated notes, 16th glides, so `slideProb` 0.7 with stepwise M2/m3/P4 intervals and only `medium` distortion, against the heavy 808s of the menace entries. Bright bell over dark 808 is the `bright_bell` timbre against a low register. ⚠ `chords.impliedByRiff` is set for the researched \"static i or i–VI\" — both families are researched here, neither is invented — and chord variety comes from `chordDurationBeats` plus three harmonic rhythms. ⚠ The percussion accents the research places on offbeats are authored only as lane presence and density: `percs` has no placement field, so the offbeat part of that claim is NOT modelled.",
